{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>He makes him ride on the high places of the earth.</b> About him it is said: 'והרכבתיך על במותי ארץ' etc." "<b>He makes him ride on the high places of the earth.</b> Heights of the earth, as in 'and you shall tread on their high places.' <b>במותי</b> — the mem has hatef-qamatz, with an extra vav." "<b>And he fed him honey from the rock.</b> This is the honey of dates that grow on the palm trees among the rocks and the mountains. Another interpretation: <b>honey from the rock</b> is bee honey, for bees bring it into the clefts of the rocks, as Rav Yosef translates: 'as bees make' — as they are swift, as in the saying, and their line extends across the height of the world, and they bring honey from mountain herbage." "<b>And oil from the flinty rock.</b> It is the nature of olive trees to grow in places of stones and rocks."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:55:05.352397243Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}